@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Sans
skinparam BoxPadding 8
skinparam roundCorner 5
skinparam maxMessageSize 200
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam noteFontSize 9

title ST-03: CRITICAL risk — Token HELD, no session created (2026-10-05)

box "Attacker" #F8CECC
participant "Attacker\n(Stolen credentials)" as A
end box

box "Core App" #DAE8FC
participant "Auth API" as CA
database "core-db" as CDB
end box

box "Detection Engine" #FFF2CC
participant "pre-token-check" as DE
participant "Detection\nPipeline" as DP
database "detection-db" as DDB
end box

A -> CA : **POST /api/v1/auth/login**\n(stolen credentials)
activate CA

CA -> CDB : SELECT users WHERE username=?
activate CDB
CDB --> CA : user record
deactivate CDB

CA -> CA : Argon2id.verify(password, hash)
alt credentials INVALID
    CA -> CDB : INSERT login_attempt\n(outcome=failure)
    CA --> A : **401 Invalid credentials**
    destroy CA
else credentials VALID
    CA -> CDB : INSERT login_attempt\n(outcome=success)
    activate CDB
    deactivate CDB

    == Risk Gate (SYNCHRONOUS, timeout 3s) ==

    CA -> DE : **POST /internal/pre-token-check**\n(user_id, ip, ua, event_id)
    activate DE

    DE -> DE : scoring pipeline\n(hour + fail_count + ML)
    note right of DE
      **CRITICAL signal detected:**
      combined >= 0.75
      → risk_level = CRITICAL
      → require_mfa = true
      → CREATE ALERT (status=open)
    end note

    DE -> DDB : INSERT alerts\n(status=open, risk_level=critical)
    activate DDB
    deactivate DDB

    DE --> CA : **200 {risk_level: critical,\nrequire_mfa: true}**
    deactivate DE

    alt require_mfa = true (HIGH / CRITICAL)

        note over CA
          **KEY CHANGE (2026-10-05):**
          NO session is created.
          NO token is issued.
          User must pass MFA first.
        end note

        CA -> CDB : UPDATE login_attempt\n(outcome=mfa_required,\nrisk_level=critical)
        activate CDB
        deactivate CDB

        CA -> CDB : UPDATE users\n(detection_mfa_once=true)
        activate CDB
        deactivate CDB

        CA --> A : **200 {mfa_required: true}**
        destroy CA

        note over A
          Attacker has NO token.
          Cannot act on the system.
          Must pass MFA (which is sent to victim email).
        end note
    end alt
end alt

== After scoring: Detection Engine sends action to Core ==

DP -> CDB : **POST /api/v1/internal/actions**\n(action=REVOKE_SESSIONS,\nidempotency_key=detection:attempt_id:REVOKE_SESSIONS)
activate CDB

CDB -> CDB : UPDATE sessions\nSET revoked_at=NOW()\nWHERE user_id=?
note right
  **REVOKE_SESSIONS** (not LOCK_USER):
  If ML was wrong (false positive),
  user re-authenticates + passes MFA.
  LOCK_USER would require admin unlock.
end note

CDB --> DP : **200 {status: applied,\ndetails: {sessions_revoked: 3}}**
deactivate CDB

legend bottom
  **Before 2026-10-05:**
  Token was created first → action came async → attacker had 1-hour window.

  **After 2026-10-05:**
  Token is HELD before it exists → attacker cannot act.

  **CRITICAL intentionally uses REVOKE_SESSIONS, NOT LOCK_USER:**
  false positives are common; LOCK_USER would block the real user.
endlegend
@enduml
